module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.protect_carve_out_reopens_the_protected_subject

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { AtCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable }

data protect_carve_out_reopens_the_protected_subject: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "protect_carve_out_reopens_the_protected_subject" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: AtCeiling { rung: MechanicallyPreventable, ceiling_reason: "mechanically preventable while writable paths are a joined string the author can still spell as instance_root." as NonEmptyStr } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a confinement that names a refused write (ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectHome=read-only) carves the protected subject back in as a writable path, so the write succeeds. DISTINGUISHING FACT: the annotation and the Protect* properties can both be true while ReadWritePaths (or an equivalent exception) is a parent of the thing they claim to refuse. HARM: a dispatched worker with --dangerously-skip-permissions writes the deployed binary or tree; the recovery cost is a dirty release, paid later at interest. Silent success is below the ladder.",

    "SPECIMEN (smart-gull-336 item c, operator plan 2026-10-13): gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator dispatch_worker_writable_paths yielded ReadWritePaths=/opt/gunbc on srv1_live_dashboard_instance (instance_root=/opt/gunbc), covering /opt/gunbc/bin and /opt/gunbc/gunbc. The module claimed a refused write; on srv1 that claim did not hold.",

    "REPAIR: ReadWritePaths is the attempt worktree, worker scratch, git objects/refs/logs/packed-refs, and only this attempt's .git/worktrees/<entry> (never the parent: sibling entries hold other attempts' commondir/gitdir, review 81064). Inside those carve-outs, ReadOnlyPaths= (no '-' prefix: systemd skips a missing '-' path, so the three files must exist at unit start, which the staged spawn's worktree-add guarantees) covers the worktree gitfile and .git/worktrees/<n>/\{commondir,gitdir\}, derived as DispatchWorkerGitPointerFiles. config.worktree is writable and inert: git reads it only when extensions.worktreeConfig is set in the common .git/config, which the worker cannot write (review 81053). belt_commit_git pins --git-dir and --work-tree, sets GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 and GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, and refuses unless the gitfile and commondir equal the derived paths — it does not run git on a mismatch. git_command_config_inert_args remains. A confined belt-commit unit (same fold, NoNewPrivileges) is feasible via a new pinned grant and is not this cut.",

    "RESIDUAL, DECLARED (review 81064): the shared ref store stays writable as a whole. git updates a ref through a <ref>.lock beside it, so refs/, logs/ and packed-refs must be writable directories, and refs/heads/dispatch/ holds every attempt's branch; a worker can move any ref, including another attempt's branch and the controller's base refs. Hooks and config stay out of reach and the controller's git runs with git_command_config_inert_args. NEXT TRIGGER for this residual: a per-attempt git directory (the worker commits into its own repository, objects borrowed from the shared store as an alternate; the controller fetches the attempt branch), after which no shared-repo path is worker-writable.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable on the carve-out class (wide ReadWritePaths). RUNG NOW: mechanically preventable on the git-pointer reopen. Dry: test.claim.roadmap.dispatch_worker_confinement_witness the_srv1_worker_cannot_write_the_deployed_binary_or_tree (ReadOnlyPaths + membership) and test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate_witness a_mismatched_gitfile_or_commondir_is_untrusted and belt_commit_git_does_not_use_a_worker_planted_hooks_path. Wet: test.claim.roadmap.dispatch_worker_writable_sandbox_wet_witness writing_the_gitfile_or_commondir_inside_the_unit_fails_and_a_worktree_commit_succeeds and belt_commit_refuses_a_planted_commondir_without_running_git. Kernel enforcement of ReadOnlyPaths still rides sandbox_properties_declared_but_not_enforced_by_the_realization until the system-manager grant is live.",

    "CEILING: mechanically preventable while writable paths are a joined string the author can still spell as instance_root. Structurally guaranteed once a typed AttemptResourceSet (or equivalent) has no constructor for the deploy tree or binary. Outside the modeled guarantee: whether systemd applies the properties at all. NEXT TRIGGER: consume Manager B's AttemptResourceSet so the deploy tree has no constructor in the worker writable set.",

    "CONSUMPTION: this per-class record joins the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.dispatch_worker_unit_confinement", decl_name: "dispatch_worker_writable_paths"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator", decl_name: "dispatch_worker_path_is_writable"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.roadmap.dispatch_worker_confinement_witness", decl_name: "the_srv1_worker_cannot_write_the_deployed_binary_or_tree"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.dispatch_worker_unit_confinement", decl_name: "dispatch_worker_git_pointer_files"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate", decl_name: "belt_commit_git_trust"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.roadmap.roadmap_belt_actuate_witness", decl_name: "a_mismatched_gitfile_or_commondir_is_untrusted"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.roadmap.dispatch_worker_writable_sandbox_wet_witness", decl_name: "writing_the_gitfile_or_commondir_inside_the_unit_fails_and_a_worktree_commit_succeeds"),
  ],
}
